<title>ITALY: Hugo Boss to open 20 shops in U.S.</title>
<headline>Hugo Boss to open 20 shops in U.S.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German fashion retailer Hugo Boss, majority owned by Italy's Marzotto group, said it aims to open 20 more shops in the United States over the next three years.</p>
<p>The company gave its intention in a statement announcing the inauguration on Tuesday of a new Boss shop in Rodeo Drive, Los Angeles which at over 400 square metres it said was the biggest in the world.</p>
<p>The group now has six shops in the United States, where Hugo Boss Fashion posted an increase in 1996 U.S. turnover of 16.6 percent, to the equivalent of 119.7 million German marks.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
